  "notes": "D89 code profile: syntax parsers for symbol, import and dependency extraction. tree-sitter is the C runtime (built by cc, already locked); the five grammar crates carry a generated parser each. All MIT; the python, javascript and typescript crates ship no LICENSE file in the .crate, so the evidence is the upstream repository file at the release tag (same text). tree-sitter default features are off (no wasm). New locked packages: the eight above; regex, serde_json and cc were already locked. Not-parsed input is bounded by the caller (1.5 MB per source file, 40 symbols and 40 imports per file).",
  "advisories": {
    "scan_recorded": true,
